  "measured_contradiction_2026_08_13": "fleet_executor.py:789-790 asserts the shared-signal gates 'apply UNIFORMLY to every arm'. The ledgers disagree: at 11:41-11:43 ET safe-2 logged SKIP_BULL_1100_1200 and took nothing, while safe-3 ENTERED at 11:42:05 on the same 775.73 trigger -- and both resolve to params.json, where the gate is present. Either the comment is stale or the gate is not applied on the fleet path. This is the THIRD stale-guarantee comment found on 2026-08-13 (the others: build_shared_signal's 'an arm can only filter further, never enter when production held', and run_cmd_hidden's 'regardless of launcher mechanism').  UNRESOLVED -- do not act on this matrix as if it were a consumption map.",
